---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import FeatureVisual from '../../components/FeatureVisual.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Workspaces"
  description="Six task-focused workspaces over one document. Logo tools live in Design, Code export is shared, and Email keeps its specialized authoring workflow."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Workspaces
      </nav>

      <h1 class="site-page-title">Workspaces</h1>
      <p class="feature-intro">
        Six task-focused workspaces over one document. Each workspace leads with the tools, panels, and
        inspector tabs its task needs — and remembers how you arrange them.
      </p>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>One document, six workspaces</h2>
        <p>
          Varve's workspaces are not separate apps or templates. Design, Print, Draw, Photo, Motion,
          and Email all operate on the same document, selection, viewport, and undo
          history — switching workspaces never forks your work, and switching back restores what
          you left. Switch from the menubar switcher, the View &gt; Workspace menu, the command
          palette, or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>1</kbd>…<kbd>5</kbd> and
          <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>7</kbd>; the active workspace is always named, and
          workspaces that don't fit stay in the switcher's overflow menu. Logo Tools and Code have
          dedicated shortcuts that reveal those shared surfaces without adding workspace tabs.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Design</strong> — UI/UX design, components, tokens, responsive layouts, prototyping, Logo tools, and developer handoff.</li>
          <li><strong>Print</strong> — multi-page layouts, typography, preflight, colour management, and production output.</li>
          <li><strong>Draw</strong> — raster painting, vector freehand, brushes.</li>
          <li><strong>Photo</strong> — nondestructive editing, retouching, selections, masking, and compositing.</li>
          <li><strong>Motion</strong> — timeline animation, keyframes, and easing.</li>
          <li><strong>Email</strong> — responsive email template authoring, email-specific preflight, and HTML export.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Explore <a href={sitePath('/features/logo')}>Logo tools in Design</a>, the dedicated
          <a href={sitePath('/features/email')}>Email authoring workflow</a>, and
          <a href={sitePath('/features/code')}>shared Code export</a>. Opening Code never switches
          workspaces. Email preview is rendered in Varve's browser surface; it does not claim
          client-by-client Gmail or Outlook verification.
        </p>
      </section>

      <FeatureVisual
        scene="workspaces"
        caption="The Print workspace on a poster document — the switcher sits in the menubar, naming the active mode and keeping the rest one icon away, and the left panel carries the Masters, Pages, and Spreads controls print work needs."
      />

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Customize once, remembered per mode</h2>
        <p>
          The Customize Workspace dialog controls every surface a workspace owns, applied instantly
          and saved per mode:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Panels</strong> — show or hide Layers, Inspector, Timeline, Resources, the shared Code panel, Logo tools, and History panels per workspace.</li>
          <li><strong>Toolbar</strong> — reorder and hide tools, including tools that live inside flyout groups such as boolean operations and retouch brushes, and choose whether the palette floats at the top or bottom of the canvas. Select, Hand, and Zoom always stay available so the canvas can never strand you.</li>
          <li><strong>Inspector tabs</strong> — visibility per workspace, with the contextual Design/Properties surface, workflow tabs such as Adjustments or Prototype, and output tabs such as Export.</li>
          <li><strong>Status bar sections</strong> — active tool, cursor position, zoom, units, layout score, preflight, and more.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Layouts persist across launches even where browser storage is unreliable, and switching
          modes saves your current panel widths to the mode you are leaving and restores the saved
          widths of the mode you enter. Show All Panels recovers an accidentally hidden layout in one
          command.
        </p>
        <p>
          The canvas minimap lives with the Layers surface when that panel is available, while its
          visibility is a separate View preference. It follows the active design canvas or publishing
          pasteboard across workspace changes and remains recoverable from View, the command palette,
          or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>M</kbd>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Safe by default</h2>
        <p>
          Customization cannot remove essential navigation, every stored preference is sanitized
          against corrupted or outdated data, Reset restores the built-in layout for the current
          mode, and Reset All asks before discarding every workspace's customizations at once.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section note">
        <h2>Collapsible floating containers & panel windows</h2>
        <p>
          Side panels elevate above the central canvas in instrument-grade opaque containers. Every panel
          features dedicated one-click collapse toggles and keyboard shortcuts, allowing instant collapse to
          reclaim full canvas canvas area. Desktop builds can also detach Layers, Inspector, Assets, Code,
          and Logo into independent windows with automatic boundary clamping.
        </p>
        <p>
          The top navigation bar features a compact, modular toolbar with context-aware shortcuts that
          dynamically adjust to selected layers, bringing critical tools and hotkeys right to your fingertips.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <h2>Pick your workspace</h2>
        <Button href={sitePath('/download')}>Download Varve</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }.feature-page h1 { font-family: var(--font-editorial); margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-intro { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-section p, .feature-section li { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .feature-section li + li { margin-top: 0.65rem; }
  .note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
